    "pressure": {
      "file": "wet_scrubber_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Energy in the throat buys efficiency",
      "description": "Gas accelerates to high velocity in the venturi throat and shatters the injected liquid into fine droplets; dust particles impact them because of the large relative velocity. Collection efficiency rises with throat pressure drop (often ≈ 25–100 mbar for fine particulate) — the fan power pays for it. The diffuser recovers part of the pressure, and the cyclonic separator then removes the dirty droplets. Wet scrubbers also cool and saturate the gas and can absorb soluble gases.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
  },
